[0.054, "o", "RFC 3161 timestamp evidence for commits\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mUsage:\u001b[0m \u001b[1mgit-time\u001b[0m [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mCommands:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1mhook\u001b[0m       Git hook entrypoint\r\n  \u001b[1mseal\u001b[0m       Seal a commit (HEAD by default) with the configured authorities\r\n  \u001b[1mdrop\u001b[0m       Leave the next commit unsealed on purpose\r\n  \u001b[1mverify\u001b[0m     Judge the evidence of commits\r\n  \u001b[1mlog\u001b[0m        List evidence per commit\r\n  \u001b[1minstall\u001b[0m    Wire the hooks into this repository\r\n  \u001b[1muninstall\u001b[0m  Unwire the hooks again and restore the ones that were displaced\r\n  \u001b[1mdoctor\u001b[0m     Report configuration and anchor health\r\n  \u001b[1mtsa\u001b[0m        Manage timestamp authorities\r\n  \u001b[1manchor\u001b[0m     Manage pinned anchor certificates\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[4mOptions:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m-C\u001b[0m <DIR>       Run in the repository at this directory instead of the current one\r\n  \u001b[1m-h\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--help\u001b[0m     Print help\r\n  \u001b[1m-V\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m--version\u001b[0m  Print version\r\n\r\nQuick start:\r\n  git time tsa select    pick authorities; each chosen anchor is pinne"]
[0.000, "o", "d\r\n  git time install       wire the hooks (git-time must be on PATH)\r\n  git commit -m \"...\"    the only command you type from then on\r\n  git time verify        judge the evidence; run it in CI\r\n\r\nEvidence is written into the commit as X-RFC3161-* trailers before the\r\ncommit lands, covered by its signature, and a commit already on a remote is\r\nleft alone. A dead authority costs evidence, never the commit.\r\n\r\n`git time doctor` names why nothing is sealing, `git time tsa select` is the\r\nrepair path, and docs/manual.md has the configuration and the failure modes.\r\n"]
